 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** The method was introduced in the paper "Learning Neural Light Fields with Ray-Space Embedding Networks" by Benjamin et al. [S1, S1, unofficial].
-*   **History:** The work was done while the first author was an intern at Meta [S1, S1, unofficial]. It addresses the limitations of prior volumetric representations, which often have large memory footprints and struggle with view-dependent effects, and the challenges of learning light fields directly from 2D slices using standard coordinate-based MLPs [S1, S1, unofficial].
-*   **Usage:** Used for view synthesis on forward-facing scenes, both dense (Stanford Light Fields) and sparse (Real Forward-Facing) [S1, S1, unofficial].
